  "product": "GTS",
  "name": "Wide Hoover Stack",
  "author": "Riddim Rack",
  "description": "A hoover-style supersaw wall: two thick stacks of heavily detuned saws that drop in pitch at the start of every note, pushed into warm overdrive and spread wide with chorus and a touch of room. Play octave leads and held lines between C3 and C5; it is mono and legato, the low end stays clear, the level stays even across the keys, and harder hits play louder and brighter. Macros: Width opens the chorus and dimension; Brightness opens the filter; Dive sets how far each note falls and opens the filter a little as it does; Chorus Depth deepens the chorus and adds shimmer.",
